Prediction Cup Trading Bot
I built these tools for Susquehanna's Predictions Cup 
(running from October 1 to November 4 of 2026); it was
a simulated prediction market trading competition on
the 2026 United States midterm elections.

Result: I finished 262nd of 1969 participants.

The project had three parts:

- An arbitrage bot which finds races where the democratic
and republican sides are mispriced against each other
and buys for a guaranteed profit

- A Senate Monte Carlo model which estimates each Senate race's
win probability and Senate control, then sizes bets where the model
disagrees with the market

- An election-night model which updates win probabilities live from partial
vote counts

THE ARBITRAGE BOT:
-scanner.py downloads every open market and its best bid/ask, pairs the Democrat and Republican buy
and reports which pairs have a guaranteed edge
-depth.py checks both order books to see how many pairs can be filled before the edge is gone
-recycler.py is the actual bot; it opens pairs when combined bids exceed 1 by at least 0.5 cents;
and it closes existing pairs early when it can sell them back for a profit

How to run (you need an API key from the competition):
You need a second key with trade permissions as well! (in .env.example: SUSQ_TRADE_API_KEY should be added as well)
scanner: finds arbitrage pairs
senate_model: runs the Monte Carlo model
recycler: run the live arbitrage bot
election_night: live projections on election night




